cell_type":"markdown","id":"9cc821fb","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036604,"end_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.482598+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.445994+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Part P — Two-model Bayesian predictive-evidence filter\n","\n","The novel-state filter and the model-probability filter are run in parallel.\n","\n","The model indicator uses fixed, predeclared transition probabilities:\n","\n","\\[\n","P(M_5(t)|M_0(t-1))=p_{05},\n","\\]\n","\n","\\[\n","P(M_0(t)|M_5(t-1))=p_{50}.\n","\\]\n","\n","These transition probabilities are not tuned on structural validation EPE; null calibration is\n","performed on the resulting posterior odds."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b26a49c0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036304,"end_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.555196+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.518892+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 46. Stable Gaussian log-likelihood and probability helpers"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":53,"id":"3789e8ac","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.628942Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.628435Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.635654Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.63491Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.045703,"end_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.63715+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.591447+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def stable_logistic(x):\n","    x = float(\n","        np.clip(\n","            x,\n","            -60.0,\n","            60.0\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","    return float(\n","        1.0\n","        / (\n","            1.0\n","            + np.exp(\n","                -x\n","            )\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def stable_logit(p):\n","    p = float(\n","        np.clip(\n","            p,\n","            CFG.probability_eps,\n","            1.0-CFG.probability_eps\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","    return float(\n","        np.log(\n","            p/(1.0-p)\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def gaussian_logpdf(\n","    x,\n","    mean,\n","    cov,\n","):\n","    x = np.asarray(\n","        x,\n","        dtype=float\n","    )\n","\n","    mean = np.asarray(\n","        mean,\n","        dtype=float\n","    )\n","\n","    C = 0.5*(\n","        np.asarray(\n","            cov,\n","            dtype=float\n","        )\n","        + np.asarray(\n","            cov,\n","            dtype=float\n","        ).T\n","    )\n","\n","    scale = float(\n","        np.trace(C)\n","        / C.shape[0]\n","    )\n","\n","    C += max(\n","        CFG.covariance_jitter_fraction\n","        * max(\n","            scale,\n","            1e-12\n","        ),\n","        1e-12\n","    ) * np.eye(\n","        C.shape[0]\n","    )\n","\n","    sign, logdet = np.linalg.slogdet(\n","        C\n","    )\n","\n","    if sign <= 0:\n","        raise RuntimeError(\n","            \"Predictive covariance is not positive definite after jitter.\"\n","        )\n","\n","    d = (\n","        x-mean\n","    )\n","\n","    quad = float(\n","        d\n","        @ np.linalg.solve(\n","            C,\n","            d\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","    k = len(x)\n","\n","    return float(\n","        -0.5*(\n","            k*np.log(\n","                2.0*np.pi\n","            )\n","            + logdet\n","            + quad\n","        )\n","    )"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5fcdb780","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.037167,"end_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.711316+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.674149+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 47. Predictive-evidence / scalar-state recursion"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":54,"id":"f421cb1e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.791063Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-03T13:32:00.790553Z","iopub.status.idle"